{"title":"Deathstalker Scorpion","html":"<article class=\"wp\"><div class=\"wp-main\"><p class=\"wp-lede\">A level 32 Scorpion that attacks with stab (melee).</p>\n      <h2>Fighting it</h2><div class=\"s\"><i>Weak</i> <span class=\"tag-chip weak\">stab</span> &nbsp; <i>Resists</i> <span class=\"tag-chip resist\">burn</span><span class=\"tag-chip resist\">corrode</span><span class=\"tag-chip resist\">slash</span></div>\n      <p class=\"s muted\">A weakness adds 30% damage and a resistance takes 30% off (the game's own rule).</p>\n      \n      <p class=\"s\">Special: carapaceFlat: 3 | venomChance: .4 | venomDamage: 20</p>\n      <h2>Levels</h2><div class=\"q-picker\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Level\"><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/deathstalker-scorpion\">All levels</a><a class=\"q-chip on\" href=\"#/monster/deathstalker-scorpion?lv=32\">Lv 32 <span>7</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/deathstalker-scorpion?lv=33\">Lv 33 <span>4</span></a><a class=\"q-chip\" href=\"#/monster/deathstalker-scorpion?lv=34\">Lv 34 <span>5</span></a></div>\n      <p class=\"s muted\">The same monster spawns at different levels, and its hitpoints, damage and XP follow its level (the game’s own formula). In the game a monster more than 5 levels above you shows its level as “???”.</p>\n      <div class=\"g-scroll\"><table class=\"g-table q-table\"><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>HP</th><th>Damage</th><th>XP</th><th>Elite (HP · dmg · XP)</th><th>Seen</th><th>Mostly</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"q-row-on\" data-href=\"#/monster/deathstalker-scorpion\" title=\"Show all levels\"><td><b>32</b> <span class=\"muted\">(base)</span></td><td>131</td><td>22.1</td><td>1,600</td><td class=\"muted\">393 · 30.9 · 4,800</td><td>7</td><td>near <a href=\"#/map/place/Dune%20Raider%20Stronghold\">Dune Raider Stronghold</a></td></tr><tr class=\"\" data-href=\"#/monster/deathstalker-scorpion?lv=33\" title=\"Pick level 33\"><td><b>33</b></td><td>137</td><td>22.7</td><td>1,650</td><td class=